## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical fairness under backpressure, observability, and controlled rollout in production.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant fairness under burst
- Backpressure and throttling strategies
- Canary rollouts and rollback criteria
- Observability: per-tenant latency, backlog, saturation
- Budget-aware incident response

## Code Example
```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(ratePerSec, capacity){
    this.rate = ratePerSec;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.last = Date.now();
  }
  tryConsume(n=1){
    const now = Date.now();
    const delta = (now - this.last)/1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + delta * this.rate);
    this.last = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n){ this.tokens -= n; return true; }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate throttle fairness in a staging canary before rollout?
- What metrics would you collect for a postmortem and how would you communicate budget impact?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes ability to design scalable, tenant-aware incident response and degradation at scale. It tests how candidates balance automated safeguards with precise human oversight and how runbooks integrate metrics, backfills, and recovery verification.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region, multi-tenant SLAs
- Degradation strategies and traffic shaping
- Cache strategy and data consistency during outages
- Canary testing, rollback criteria, post-incident validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo per-tenant degradation switch
function route(request){
  const t = request.tenant;
  if (t.degradation === 'high') return routeToCacheOnly();
  return routeToFullPath();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate this runbook in a synthetic outage? 
- Which dashboards and alerting thresholds would you use for tenants at risk?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to manage tenant-level reliability with shared budgets and fast containment.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant SLOs and error budgets
- Tenant-scoped routing and feature flags
- Tenant-level telemetry and alerting
- Safe rollback and RCA

## Code Example
```javascript
// tenant routing middleware sketch
function tenantRouter(req, res, next) {
  const tenant = req.headers["x-tenant-id"];
  const degraded = global.degradedTenants?.has(tenant);
  if (degraded) req.degraded = true;
  next();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate detection of affected tenants during outages?
- How do you prevent cascading alerts while preserving SLA guarantees?
